Mark the macOS engine starting recording again by itself

WebRTC patch 0014 aligns the echo controller again when the audio device module starts
recording again by itself in a call. WebRTC-SDK's AudioEngineDevice marks it
(MarkAudioDeviceRestarted) when it starts an engine that records while recording was
asked for before the change and still is: a restart or a new engine for another output
or input chosen (by its own SetPlayoutDevice or SetRecordingDevice, or by the plugin's
FogataPlayout, which takes the input away and gives it back around the devices it gives
the engine: the request is what counts, not whether the input is available), a change
of the system's default output or input, playout starting or stopping while it records,
and the end of an interruption; and when it starts the engine again around the system's
change of its configuration (ReconfigureEngine, which stops it and starts it again in
two steps). Not marked: a first start, asked for by the audio state (a call's start, a
microphone turned on again: Fogata turns the microphone on again by starting recording,
so an unmute is never one), which restarts the echo controller already, and the manual
rendering mode, which plays nothing into a room. Playout started right after recording
starts is marked, and aligns the echo controller once more, one block later.

--- a/modules/audio_device/audio_engine_device.mm
+++ b/modules/audio_device/audio_engine_device.mm
@@ -1683,6 +1683,11 @@
     if (recover_result != 0) {
       LOGE() << "ReconfigureEngine: Failed to recover engine state, error: " << recover_result;
       // We're in a bad state now, could consider more recovery options here
+    } else if (current_state.IsInputRunning()) {
+      // Fogata: stopped and started again around the system's change of the
+      // engine's configuration, recording with it (WebRTC patch 0014).
+      LOGI() << "ReconfigureEngine: recording started again";
+      MarkAudioDeviceRestarted();
     }
   }));
 }
@@ -3035,6 +3040,18 @@
       }
 
       if (start_result) {
+        // Fogata: recording asked for before and after, and running again in an
+        // engine started anew (another device chosen, the default one changed, the
+        // input given back after the plugin took it away, the end of an
+        // interruption): the echo controller aligns again (WebRTC patch 0014). The
+        // request, not whether the input is available: the plugin takes the input
+        // away and gives it back around a device it chooses. A first start, asked
+        // for by the audio state, is not one.
+        if (state.prev.input_running && state.next.input_running &&
+            state.next.IsInputRunning()) {
+          LOGI() << "Recording started again with the engine";
+          MarkAudioDeviceRestarted();
+        }
         rollback_actions.push_back([this]() {
           RTC_DCHECK_RUN_ON(thread_);
           LOGI() << "Rolling back engine start (Device)...";
